- Asking EJ to write the vision and requirements concentrates the work on EJ — bottleneck (#8 value victory, not duration? maybe not). Cost: if the vision is EJ's and EJ is the bottleneck, the AI cannot proceed; #11 pay for foreknowledge from people — the price is paying (time) for the people who know.
- Letting AI write the vision would violate the one-maker rule and #11 (foreknowledge must come from people who know the situation, not likeness to past events) — cost: a plausible vision not tied to the user.

