- Run one requirement two ways: (A) write/freeze the requirement's units first, then generate cases; (B) generate cases first from "brainstorm every scenario", then derive units. Compare: does (B) change any unit or add a "fails if"? If (B) adds/changes units, "use cases first" holds for discovery at least sometimes; if it adds none but changes the count, it broke. Also: take the planted-violation test — the old-case set must fail once. (#1: by this I know victory and defeat; #17 the probe; #6 harm.)
